OK, the major trouble is that IE does not support an "onchanged" event
for checkboxes. This is why the collapsing code wasn't being called,
also. The basic method you have in there for hiding the element does
work in IE, it just wasn't being fired.

Reportedly, Safari does not support an onchanged event for checkboxes
either; and reportedly, not supporting one is HTML 4.0 compliant.
Firefox is being too lenient.

After changing "onchanged" to "onclick" for all checkbox items in the
page, another problem presents itself. Even though you provided only a
name, not an id, for the checkboxes, getElementById is still finding
the checkbox named 'attack' when what is wanted is the table named
'attack'.  Changing all the table names to have a prefix of t_ will fix
this. The resulting HTML works in both IE6 and in Firefox.



